{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/117653-cold-iron-hand-forged-iron-meteoric-iron","id":117653,"title":"Cold iron, hand forged iron, meteoric iron","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-22T14:40:13-07:00","id":117653,"title":"Cold iron, hand forged iron, meteoric iron","content":"I think i had something confused in my mind before. When i first read the core book, i didnt understand that cold iron and hand forged iron were two different things. Then I read some other of the books that talked about literally hand forging it, using no hammer nor tool, by the us of a special kith and when you find the metal heated such because a meteorite landed and you were around there to mold it. Now I am just confused. What exactly does it take for an iron to be considered cold iron? What does it take for it to be considered hand forged iron? Is there any hand forged iron other than a meteoric iron? Because I have a blacksmithing ogre that can make iron weapons himself with his 4dots in crafts and 4 in strength, given the usual appropiate tools to forge, he time, and such, and I imagined what he did as being cold iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T14:47:07-07:00","id":117658,"title":"","content":"Cold iron is iron that has not been enchanted, shaped, conjured, or otherwise altered with magic. Hand-forged iron is cold iron that has not even been shaped by human-held fire but by raw force. Meteoric iron is a form of cold iron that is particularly sought-after because the heat of atmospheric entry has smelted the ore naturally, thus negating the need to work with cheats like the one added to the Smith kith blessing in Rites of Spring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-22-2014, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:04:44-07:00","id":117672,"title":"","content":"Hand forged iron then would need to be iron-ore unless meteoric? And even then it would almost always look like a weird rock thing? I would imagine imagine it with durability 1 or something like that, as breakable as a rock. Idk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:03:10-07:00","id":117710,"title":"","content":"I usually just go with cold iron being reasonably pure iron worked by hammer and muscle, without magic or mass-production tools, like casts and stuff.<br /> <br /> Makes it a bit easier to get, but eh, players seem to have fun with it. Not super-powerful anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T21:26:56-07:00","id":117842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/117653-cold-iron-hand-forged-iron-meteoric-iron?p=117710#post117710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually just go with cold iron being reasonably pure iron worked by hammer and muscle, without magic or mass-production tools, like casts and stuff. Makes it a bit easier to get, but eh, players seem to have fun with it. Not super-powerful anyway</div> </div> </div> </div> Thats more or less my current understanding. What I am not following is how &quot;easily&quot; could you do a hand forger iron weapon. I mean, if I understand correctly, it would. Be something made from iron ore and by being hit without ANY heat... It would break if hit too much anyways... So its not like you can do almost anything with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T09:04:52-07:00","id":117938,"title":"","content":"If I recall right ROS says you need a Strength of 4 to hand forge raw iron without the use of a forge. Simply you, a hammer, an anvil, and the lump of ore. Without the fire you keep all of the awesome properties (agg. to True Fae, negates fairy mojo it comes in contact with, folds your laundry...) but it's hard work. The Smith kith gets its little cheat which is kinda neat, but I personally dislike it on the simple grounds that you are using fairy magic to work something utterly immune to fairy magic. Still, could make an awesome story that Iron isn't too pissed at Smiths.<br /> <br /> Also, from our game, I've found have a pouch of iron filings is much easier to have on hand. And making arrowheads is a lot more simple than making a knife or sword. Our game is historical, so the arrows aren't really out of place and they only come out when we need them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2546-jaellot","name":"jaellot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T11:55:36-07:00","id":118031,"title":"","content":"I really think they've gone too far with the whole cold iron thing. Personally, I've had fun where a game had anything made of iron, including steel, counted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T06:54:19-07:00","id":118402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jaellot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/117653-cold-iron-hand-forged-iron-meteoric-iron?p=117938#post117938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall right ROS says you need a Strength of 4 to hand forge raw iron without the use of a forge. Simply you, a hammer, an anvil, and the lump of ore. Without the fire you keep all of the awesome properties (agg. to True Fae, negates fairy mojo it comes in contact with, folds your laundry...) but it's hard work. The Smith kith gets its little cheat which is kinda neat, but I personally dislike it on the simple grounds that you are using fairy magic to work something utterly immune to fairy magic. Still, could make an awesome story that Iron isn't too pissed at Smiths. Also, from our game, I've found have a pouch of iron filings is much easier to have on hand. And making arrowheads is a lot more simple than making a knife or sword. Our game is historical, so the arrows aren't really out of place and they only come out when we need them.</div> </div> </div> </div> So that would supposedly be hand forged iron? What confuses me is that if its iron ore, wouldnt it break with hammering as any rock would? And if its iron iron and not iron ore, well, then it has gone through human held fire then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T04:44:26-07:00","id":120287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Cold iron is short for cold wrought iron. IE Iron once smelted that is worked without heat which has advantages and drawbacks,. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://blog.heritage-metalworks.com/2011/05/rod-iron-rot-iron-wrought-ironbut.html&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://blog.heritage-metalworks.com/...t-ironbut.html</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrought_iron\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrought_iron</a></div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but I think this is exactly the kind of unnecessary homework stuff that doesn't belong in a game. I also think that, while allowing steel to count as iron and ignoring all the special snowflake kinds of iron is a houserule, it's one with interesting effects upon the changeling game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:03:21-07:00","id":121749,"title":"","content":"Technically, &quot;Cold Iron&quot; is a poetic term. It has no meaning beyond sounding pretty. Like &quot;cold hard cash.&quot; Cold Iron in literature and folklore can refer to be both metal or steel and I cannot think of any reference outside of modern fantasy and roleplaying games that make note of any special processing (or lack thereof) that is necessary to confer it's magical properties against the supernatural.<br /> <br /> However, the rules in the game are very specific when it comes to outlining what &quot;Cold Iron&quot; is, in the context of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T03:43:48-07:00","id":122259,"title":"","content":"I am still confused <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> can someone. Pllease specifically tell me? Like, iron to be iron and not iron ore needs to be heated by handheld fire at least once anyways. So far the only thing i get is that dirctly blacksmithing iron without supernatural means gives me cold iron. The rest still confuses me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:36:57-07:00","id":122350,"title":"","content":"Using real world logic and metallurgy does not apply to &quot;Cold Iron&quot; in the context of Changeling: The Lost. In &quot;Rites of Spring&quot; there are several pages devoted to Iron, its different manifestations and its effect on fairies. Only iron that has not been heated by a man-made fire or manipulated via magic counts as &quot;Cold Iron.&quot; Other types of iron (pig iron, wrought iron, etc etc) still affect fairies in different ways, but not to the same extent that the mythical &quot;Cold Iron&quot; is known for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T19:12:41-07:00","id":122854,"title":"","content":"Kind of lame for someone to delete my posts w/o an explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T06:42:23-07:00","id":125143,"title":"","content":"I guess you to smelt your iron ore and forge you cold iron weapon in a volcano.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T09:44:17-07:00","id":127543,"title":"","content":"Something that got me through a lot of these same issues is asking the question, &quot;Is it Iron?&quot; Noticed how I capitolized that. Many things would be considered iron or to have iron in them, but to be Iron proper it has to be the pure elemental metal. For example, iron ore has many of the properties of Iron in regards to the Fae, but it isn't exactly Iron until it's been smelted. Once it's been made into &quot;reasonably pure&quot; Iron that is when you have to be delicate with it or else it could be ruined. A Smith has more options, because their Kith blessing says they know how to apply just a little bit of heat in order to make Hand Forged Iron that much more easily, meaning they get to bend the rules a little. Anything more dramatic and it loses the benefits of being Hand Forged to being Cold Iron (it is still pure iron, after all), so if it is cast into a mold, forged, tempered, etc., it is a little less effective. Once it is called something else though, like mixing in some carbon to make it steel, it isn't iron at all anymore. Anything that is naturally smelted, like meteoric Iron or the above example of a volcano, that would still count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I ask for so little. Just fear me, <b>love me</b>, do as I say and I will be your slave.<br /> -Jareth, Goblin King","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2846-jhornb02","name":"jhornb02","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2846_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T14:37:36-07:00","id":127737,"title":"","content":"the way i understand it iron and cold iron are the same thing. It is something primarily composed of iron (e.g. wrought iron) which has not been enchanted, shaped, conjured, or otherwise altered with magic and bypasses fae defenses. Then you have Hand forged iron which meets the preceding requirements and has not been heated or smelted by human hands (e.g.) meteoric iron and that does agg to the true fae. ill admit though it did take me a few times to get it too lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1445-elesho","name":"elesho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}